;; The check harness's time (seon.check; docs/clocks.md "a check's measurement, and a check's ping").
{
 ;; Unit: ms a check's Flow ping (seon.check/ping) waits for a proc to take its control message,
 ;; which a proc takes between two steps. Provenance: 2026-10-22; the pings it replaced waited 1000 and 2000 ms and read a miss as nil or
 ;; :unknown, and a check beside a full bin/test must not mistake a slow step for a missing
 ;; proc. At the bound: the proc is recorded {:blocked pid :ping-ms ..} in the check's report
 ;; and the check that read it fails, naming it.
 :seon.config.check/ping-ms [:int {:default 10000 :min 1 :seon.config/unit "ms" :description "How long a check's Flow ping waits for a proc to take its control message; past it the proc is recorded :blocked."}]
 ;; Unit: times. A check step's bound, this many times its median measured run (its greens' :ms, seon.fx/typical-ms), floored
 ;; at :seon.config.agent/stall-ms: what seon.proofs/step-bounds answers (no script ends a run on it). Provenance: of 6,239 green
 ;; runs in the verdict cache of tests whose median is 2 s or more, 161 ran past 5 times it and 30 (0.5%) past 10, most
 ;; at load 30-40 before proves took slots; past 10 is a hang more often than a slow machine.
 :seon.config.check/step-end-factor [:int {:default 10 :min 2 :seon.config/unit "times" :description "A check step's bound in times its median measured run, floored at :seon.config.agent/stall-ms (seon.proofs/step-bounds); no script ends a run on it."}]
 ;; Unit: ms over which a check measures that something does not happen: a paused agent's
 ;; request unanswered (lifecycle). Provenance: the windows it replaced were 300, 400 and 500 ms.
 ;; Load only makes what it measures likelier. At the bound: the measurement is read.
 :seon.config.check/hold-ms [:int {:default 500 :min 1 :seon.config/unit "ms" :description "The window over which a check measures that something does not happen (a paused agent's request unanswered)."}]
 ;; Unit: ms between the readings scale-work takes of the machine's available memory and of each process
 ;; under root's fork server while its agents work (seon.check/scale-work). Provenance: a footprint
 ;; reading of ~25 processes takes ~100-300 ms; the window is what the test children's peaks are caught
 ;; within, a measurement and never a dependency. At the bound: the reading is taken again.
 :seon.config.check/sample-ms [:int {:default 200 :min 1 :seon.config/unit "ms" :description "The window between scale-work's readings of the machine's available memory and of its processes' footprints (a measurement, never a dependency)."}]}
